# Rust
**/target/
corpus/generate/out/

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# CI (hyper-pack-nuget.yml) arranges and packs these per-RID at pack time; regenerable
# locally via `cargo cdylib` (the csproj's runtimes/**/native/* wildcard item).
csharp/HyperTabular/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperTabular/staticlibs/

# PHP
# Native libs under php/src/native/{rid}/ are not ignored: as in HyperCast, Packagist has no
# packing step — the git tree at the tag IS the package — so the libraries a release ships
# are committed there. Without one for the platform, the binding falls back to
# rust/target/release/ (`cargo cdylib`).
php/vendor/
php/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# The root composer.json exists only for Packagist, which reads the repository root; nothing
# here runs `composer install` from the root, and a stray local one should not be committed.
/vendor/
/composer.lock

# Swift
# The static libraries under swift/HyperTabularCore.artifactbundle/{triple}/, and the
# info.json that lists them, are not ignored — as in HyperCast, where they are committed,
# because SwiftPM has no packing step for a git-URL dependency, and only by
# stage-native-binaries.yml, after their provenance checks. Until this repository has that
# workflow none is in the tree: the forge's static-libs/build-static-libs.sh builds them
# (CI runs it before every Swift step), and a developer's own build of them shows up as
# untracked and is not to be committed by hand.
**/.build/
# A library's pins are its consumers' to make: HyperCast is resolved fresh from the range
# the manifests declare, by CI as by anyone depending on this package.
/Package.resolved
/swift/Package.resolved
/swift/StaticSmokeTest/Package.resolved
